+# Failure signatures
+
+| Symptom                                                     | Likely cause                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
+| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Default persists but is not selected at runtime             | Check whether initialization received missing/invalid data or an explicit clear; inspect default hydration and the runtime CVA before changing precedence.                                                                                            |
+| Builder selection appears in saved `formData`               | Builder interaction is emitting a normal field value instead of updating renderer configuration and clearing the data entry.                                                                                                                          |
+| Required flag is saved but no asterisk appears              | The component library does not render a required marker for that field type; add it in the application renderer.                                                                                                                                      |
+| Required submit validation does nothing                     | The rendered control lacks the library validation attribute, is not registered with the Angular form, or the form handler cannot locate its named host element.                                                                                       |
+| Submit error remains after correcting a field               | A nested value accessor may have emitted before `NgModel` committed the new value, or only the Angular errors were cleared; refresh the changed field through `refreshValidationMessages`.                                                            |
+| Repeated interaction displays duplicate validation messages | The form handler is creating a new error element on each refresh, often because it is resolving an unrecognized wrapper instead of the existing shared control; correct the DOM control identity and make refresh setup reuse the existing container. |
+| `Cannot access property "tagName", formElement is null`     | A registered control either lacks the host `[attr.name]` needed for lookup or is temporarily unmounted; check control identity first, then ensure DOM-dependent library code handles absent elements safely.                                          |
+| Disabled field can still be cleared or changed              | Disabled state reached the primary input but not a nested clear/suffix action or keyboard path; propagate effective disabled state and guard the action callback.                                                                                     |
+| Option removal leaves a selection/default behind            | Option changes are not validating and clearing both configured defaults and stale current values.                                                                                                                                                     |
+| Add button is clipped by the scrollbar                      | The option-row grid has no reserved action width or the content column is not constrained with `minmax(0, 1fr)`.                                                                                                                                      |
+| Placeholder appears as submitted data                       | Placeholder text was wired as a value/default instead of as display-only control metadata.                                                                                                                                                            |
+| Rule enable loses field configuration                       | Disabled-rule application rebuilt the renderer without spreading the existing configuration.                                                                                                                                                          |
